## Learn Your Rights Under Lemon Law

Modesto might not have anything on San Francisco traffic, but you still need a reliable vehicle to get around Stanislaus County. The last thing you want to deal with is a car that has irreparable, manufacturer-related issues.

Lemon cars are created by shoddy manufacturing practices. No matter how you squeeze them, they’re a sour car - and you shouldn’t have to deal with that, especially if you bought them from a responsible seller. That’s why the California lemon law exists.

The Song Beverly Consumer Warranty Act (California lemon law) protects drivers throughout the state who wind up behind the wheel of a lemon car. It holds manufacturers accountable for selling cars that shouldn’t ever be given to unwitting drivers. At CLINE APC, our Modesto lemon law attorneys uphold this law by helping victims receive fair compensation for their trouble with lemon vehicles.

These factors indicate if manufacturer mistakes entitle you to compensation under California lemon law:

- The vehicle manufacturer has made at least two or more attempts to repair a warranty-covered defect, or

- The vehicle has been out of service for more than 30 days while being repaired for warranty-covered problems; and

- The vehicle has several warranty-covered problems, which were not caused by abuse of the vehicle and that impair its use, value, or safety.

It’s important to note that there is a time limit for seeking compensation under Modesto, California lemon law, even with the aid of a lemon lawyer in Modesto. Your lemon car’s defect must occur within the defined terms of the manufacturer or dealer warranty.

Despite the common misunderstanding, your vehicle’s issue does not need to be addressed within the first 18 months after purchase or before the odometer reaches 18,000 miles. The 18-month / 18,000-mile window is a lemon-law presumption, not a requirement. It does not decide whether you have a good case. What matters is whether the defect first occurred during the original manufacturer warranty.

When your vehicle meets California lemon law requirements, you’re entitled to:

Manufacturer coverage of your Modesto lemon law lawyer and court costs A full refund of the vehicle’s original acquisition price and incidental costs A replacement vehicle if necessary The process of obtaining your [lemon buyback value](/tool/buyback-calculator) is not always simple. For consumers who don’t seek out the help of a specialized [lemon lawyer California](/), manufacturers will often create unnecessary hurdles or openly deny your rights.

